G2908.def:
κρείσσων
(Epic and old Att..) and κρείττων (later Att..), prop. comparat. of κρατύς, strong, but in sense often (as in cl., see LS, see word) as comparat. of ἀγαθός, [in LXX chiefly for טוֹב ;] 
better; 
__(a) as to ad­vantage or usefulness: 1 Corinthiens 11:17, Hébreux 11:40 12:24; πολλῷ μᾶλλον κ., Philippiens 1:23; κρεῖσσον ποιεῖν, 1 Corinthiens 7:38; ἐστιν, before inf., 1 Corinthiens 7:9, 2 Pierre 2:21; 
__(b) as to excellence: Hébreux 1:4 6:9 7:7, 19 7:22 8:6 9:23 10:34 11:16, 35; κ. ἐστι, before inf., 1 Pierre 3:17.†

G2948.def:
κυλλός, -ή, -όν 
__1. crooked, crippled: Matthieu 15:30-31 (WH, txt. om.); 
__2. maimed: Matthieu 18:8, Marc 9:43.†
